[E0420] Error: `@opaque` belongs on an `extern struct`
   ╭─[ err/133_opaque_struct/main.wip:6:1 ]
   │
 6 │ @opaque
   │ ───┬───
   │    ╰───── not a C type
   │
   │ Note: it says C knows where the fields are, which is only true of a struct C declares
───╯
[E0420] Error: `@opaque` needs the header that declares the struct
    ╭─[ err/133_opaque_struct/main.wip:11:1 ]
    │
 11 │ @opaque
    │ ───┬───
    │    ╰───── no header to read it from
    │
    │ Help: write `@header("config.h")` beside it
    │
    │ Note: the C that reaches its fields is compiled against that header, since Wip does not know where they are
────╯
[E0425] Error: `Config` is laid out by C, so a value cannot have its type
    ╭─[ err/133_opaque_struct/main.wip:23:12 ]
    │
 18 │ extern struct Config {
    │               ───┬──
    │                  ╰──── declared `@opaque` here
    │
 23 │ fn held(c: Config): c_uint = c.mode
    │            ───┬──
    │               ╰──── not a type a value can have
    │
    │ Help: a pointer to one is written `ptr<Config>`, and its fields are read through it
    │
    │ Note: `@opaque` says where the fields are is C's business, so how large one is, is too
────╯
[E0425] Error: `Config` is laid out by C, so Wip cannot make one
    ╭─[ err/133_opaque_struct/main.wip:26:16 ]
    │
 18 │ extern struct Config {
    │               ───┬──
    │                  ╰──── declared `@opaque` here
